# Input graph for RDFLib__rdflib-leveldb__test_test_functionality.py__testUpdateWithInitNs — written during translation.
#
# The region under test performs an INSERT DATA into the named graph
# <urn:graph> and then reads that same named graph back — the "read" this
# fixture exercises is really "the write did not leak elsewhere and did not
# pick up unrelated data", not a traversal of pre-existing data.  So this
# fixture supplies neighbouring triples in the DEFAULT graph (a distinct
# graph from <urn:graph>) that must NOT show up in the region's result, and
# leaves <urn:graph> itself empty before the update (the zero-solution case
# for that graph).
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .

ex:someone ex:likes ex:coffee .
